<main class="publishers" id="publishers-content">
<div class="pub-wrap">
  <header class="pub-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="pub-label">Bonfire for Publishers</p>
      <h1>Give your readers a place to belong.</h1>
      <p class="pub-intro pub-muted">Bring readers and your editorial team together in a community under your own brand, connected to your articles and memberships.</p>
      <div class="pub-actions"><a class="pub-button" href="https://cal.com/bonfire-networks/meet">Let’s talk about your publication</a><a class="pub-link" href="#jacobin">See it at Jacobin</a></div>
      <p class="pub-caption">Ghost projects from €8,000. Other publishing systems welcome.</p>
    </div>
    <figure><img class="pub-shot" src="/img/jacobin/ghostbonfire.png" width="2906" height="1729" alt="Jacobin’s publication and Bonfire community, with a consistent visual identity" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption class="pub-caption">Jacobin’s German-language edition · publication and community, connected.</figcaption></figure>
  </header>
  <div class="pub-band pub-muted"><span>Connected to your publication</span><span>Your brand, your community rules</span><span>Open source and portable</span></div>
  <section class="pub-section pub-split" aria-labelledby="participation-title">
    <div><p class="pub-label">From readership to participation</p><h2 id="participation-title">For readers who want to be part of the story.</h2></div>
    <div class="pub-copy pub-muted"><p>Your readers have ideas, questions and knowledge to share. Some already meet at your events, support your work or ask for ways to get involved.</p><p>Give that participation a home: a place to meet other readers, speak with the newsroom and keep a conversation going between articles.</p><p>Bonfire works best when your editorial team wants to take part, with someone responsible for making the community a welcoming, active place.</p></div>
  </section>
</div>
<section class="pub-section pub-case" id="jacobin" aria-labelledby="jacobin-title">
  <div class="pub-wrap pub-split">
    <div><p class="pub-label">Built with Jacobin</p><h2 id="jacobin-title">Their readers asked for a community. Together, we built it.</h2><div class="pub-copy pub-muted" style="margin-top:24px"><p>Readers wanted a protected space to discuss, bring ideas to the editorial team and see behind the scenes. Jacobin chose to build that space on infrastructure it controls.</p><p>We connected its Ghost publication with Bonfire and shaped a shared visual identity across the two sites.</p></div><a class="pub-link" href="https://jacobin.de/social/">Read Jacobin’s own story ↗</a></div>
    <div><ul class="pub-list" style="margin-top:0"><li><strong>One member relationship</strong><span class="pub-muted">Membership tiers connected to community access, with single sign-on.</span></li><li><strong>Articles and conversations together</strong><span class="pub-muted">An imported archive and linked discussions on the publication and in Bonfire.</span></li><li><strong>A space with Jacobin’s identity</strong><span class="pub-muted">Custom branding, groups, topics and community widgets.</span></li><li><strong>The newsroom takes part</strong><span class="pub-muted">Journalists and editors are directly involved in the community.</span></li></ul><a class="pub-link" href="/case-studies/jacobin/">Explore the full case study →</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="pub-wrap">
<section class="pub-section" aria-labelledby="build-title">
  <p class="pub-label">A project we build with you</p><h2 id="build-title">From your first conversation to your community’s launch.</h2>
  <div class="pub-scope">
    <article><h3>A structure for your community</h3><p class="pub-muted">We work with your team on groups, topics, member access and the experience you want readers to have.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Your publication, connected</h3><p class="pub-muted">For Ghost, we connect the existing integration, import your articles and configure memberships and access. For other systems, we agree the integration your publication needs.</p></article>
    <article><h3>A familiar identity</h3><p class="pub-muted">A custom theme, interface and agreed widgets carry your publication’s branding into its community space.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Ready to welcome readers</h3><p class="pub-muted">Configuration, agreed revisions, testing and launch guidance are part of the project. We plan the rollout with your team.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="pub-section pub-split" style="border-top:1px solid #ffffff20" aria-labelledby="ownership-title">
  <div><p class="pub-label">Autonomy comes with it</p><h2 id="ownership-title">Your community stays under your control.</h2><p class="pub-muted" style="margin-top:24px">You choose who runs the infrastructure and who helps it evolve. Bonfire is open source, so you can keep using and adapting it with the partner you choose.</p></div>
  <div><ul class="pub-list" style="margin-top:0"><li><strong>Take your community with you</strong><span class="pub-muted">With our cooperative hosting partner, ongoing backups and access to your instance’s database and files let you move to another provider.</span></li><li><strong>Members can export their own data</strong><span class="pub-muted">Individual data export is available directly in the interface.</span></li><li><strong>Your publishing system is your choice</strong><span class="pub-muted">Ghost has a proven integration. Other CMS and membership systems can be scoped with us.</span></li></ul></div>
</section>
<section class="pub-section pub-split" id="project" aria-labelledby="price-title">
  <div class="pub-offer"><p class="pub-label">Start with the proven Ghost integration</p><h2 id="price-title">Your community, built with you.</h2><p class="pub-price">From €8,000</p><p class="pub-muted">For a Ghost implementation using our existing integration, with custom branding, agreed widgets, article import, configuration, testing and launch guidance.</p><p class="pub-muted" style="margin-top:18px">We agree the scope and quote before work begins. Hosting and ongoing support are quoted separately.</p><div class="pub-actions"><a class="pub-button" href="https://cal.com/bonfire-networks/meet">Discuss your project</a></div></div>
  <div class="pub-copy"><h3>Using a different CMS?</h3><p class="pub-muted" style="margin-top:16px">Ghost is a starting point, not a requirement. Tell us how you publish and manage memberships. We’ll work out the integration, scope and cost with you.</p><a class="pub-link" href="/ghost/">Explore the Ghost integration →</a><h3 style="margin-top:34px">A technical partner after launch</h3><p class="pub-muted" style="margin-top:16px">We can provide maintenance and technical support, coordinate releases with your hosting provider and develop new features to an agreed scope.</p><p class="pub-muted">Your team leads the editorial participation, moderation and day-to-day community management. We look after the technical work agreed with you.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="pub-section" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
  <h2 id="questions-title">Before we begin.</h2>
  <div class="pub-faq">
    <details><summary>Do we need to change how we publish?</summary><p>With Ghost, your newsroom keeps its publishing workflow. Bonfire connects articles and memberships to a community space. Other systems need an integration assessment; we’ll discuss that before quoting.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can we start with a small group of readers?</summary><p>Yes. We can plan an initial rollout with a core group and configure access around it. Your team can learn how the space works before inviting a wider audience.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can conversations appear below our articles?</summary><p>Yes. The Telling connects embedded article comments with discussions in Bonfire. The comment widget can be used on different websites; deeper membership and publishing integrations are scoped separately. <a class="pub-link" href="/telling/">See how The Telling works →</a></p></details>
    <details><summary>Who hosts the community?</summary><p>You can work with our cooperative hosting partner or choose your own infrastructure and provider. We agree the hosting arrangement and technical responsibilities with you. Hosting costs are separate from the implementation project.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What if we need something new?</summary><p>We discuss the requirement, feasibility and cost with you. New features and integrations beyond the agreed launch scope are quoted separately, so you know what the project includes.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="pub-section pub-close" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><h2 id="contact-title">What would your readers like to do together?</h2><p class="pub-muted">Tell us about your publication, how readers participate today and what you want to make possible. We’ll explore whether Bonfire is a good fit.</p><div class="pub-actions"><a class="pub-button" href="https://cal.com/bonfire-networks/meet">Talk with the Bonfire team</a></div></section>
</div>
</main>
